{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The target's central claim—that coverage debt grows 'at least quadratically'—contradicts its own mechanism description. It states each new rival position requires O(k) criticism tasks where k = number of active schools. The problem context specifies 'frozen provider seats,' so k is effectively constant, making total criticism work O(n·k) = O(n), linear in the number of rivals. The quadratic prediction (option A in the simulation) requires 'unbounded per-position warrant requirements,' which directly contradicts the bounded O(k) mechanism the target itself describes. The target never explains how quadratic growth arises from its own stated mechanism, undermining its headline finding.","counterexample":[{"n":60,"k":5,"warrants_per_position":5,"total_warrants":300,"growth_class":"linear"}],"target_alias":"SRC_001"},{"attack":true,"case":"The target asserts O(N²) growth because 'per-target warrants for every pair creates a combinatorial' explosion, but per-target warrants are per-target—each target receives its own warrants— not pairwise between all targets. This misrepresents the documented mechanism. Additionally, the counterconditions reference 'SRC_004' and 'SRC_007'; SRC_007 is not a listed target in this batch, and the problem context requires grounding claims in evidence block ids, neither of which are cited. The optimization claim ('reduce coverage debt to near-linear') is asserted without any simulation to verify it, despite the problem context requiring a sandboxed Python simulation for testable numerical claims about coverage dynamics.","counterexample":null,"target_alias":"SRC_002"},{"attack":true,"case":"The target makes quantitative claims about backlog dynamics—'throughput drops to near zero as the number of active items grows, trapping the system in an unproductive attractor'—and proposes a 'desk-reject' triage transfer claim whose effect on throughput is numerically testable, yet proposes no sandboxed Python simulation (simulation_mode sandboxed_python_v1) as the problem context explicitly requires. source_memory_refs cite 'SRC_007' and 'SRC_008,' neither of which is a listed target, and no evidence block ids are cited to ground the mechanism claims.","counterexample":null,"target_alias":"SRC_003"},{"attack":true,"case":"The target proposes 'exponential' attention scaling with duration but provides no justification for why exponential—rather than linear, polynomial, or logarithmic—is the appropriate functional form. Its own countercondition concedes the proposal may cause 'pathological oscillation' where the system 'alternately abandons all new generation to retire a backlog, and then swings back to unchecked generation,' yet the target offers no damping mechanism or guardrail to prevent this admitted failure mode. The claim that an equilibrium will be 'stable' is numerically testable but no sandboxed simulation is proposed, and no evidence block ids ground the characterization of the current mechanism.","counterexample":null,"target_alias":"SRC_004"}]}